  "description": "Runs Microsoft.Data.Sqlite (and Entity Framework Core on top of it) inside a browser WebAssembly app, with the database persisted across reloads. The database file lives in the WASM runtime's in-memory filesystem; this package restores it from IndexedDB at boot and writes it back on a schedule and on page-hide, using SQLite's Online Backup API (never an unsafe file copy) via Rask.SQLite.Snapshots. A Web Lock elects one tab as the owner, so several open tabs cannot write over each other. Register `AddRaskBrowserSqlite(\"app\")` and point your DbContext at `BrowserSqlite.ConnectionString(\"app\")` — the same registration you would write on the server. Add `UseRaskFullTextSearch()` from Rask.SQLite.EntityFrameworkCore and Rask.Data's full-text search (`HasFullTextSearch`, `Search(text)`) runs on FTS5 in the browser too.",
  "iconFile": "rask-icon.png",
